{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Reproduced 2026-11-23 PST on gerrit main 053604a2618 with real exception chains (ModelAPIError <- anthropic.APIConnectionError <- httpx.ProxyError 403 <- httpcore.ProxyError), alone and as 2 legs of a FallbackExceptionGroup: both RETRY_NOW, retryable, 'Transient connection blip', diagnostic without any proxy mention. Implemented in local commit 25c97fe795f (worktree bug-f8d9-proxy-refusal): both now CHANGE_SETTINGS, non-retryable, error_type proxy_refused, proxy text in the diagnostic message, and message_for returns the proxy-refusal message. Beyond the plan: close_gate_remedy also returns the proxy message for that outcome; without it the close gate would tell the operator to install the agents extra and set an API key, because it maps every CHANGE_SETTINGS to UNAVAILABLE_REMEDY. Red check: 7 of the 13 new tests fail on the pre-fix code; the 6 that pass there are the unchanged-behaviour guards (ConnectError/ConnectTimeout, plain ModelAPIError, proxy 5xx, retryable leg wins, cause cycle). _map complexity 14 -> 13; lint, typecheck and ratchets exit 0; make verify running."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795429223311135001,"uuid":"db5684fc-ab39-48a1-b396-9c7f279c907c"}